        "id": 8510,
        "name": "Limbo_22",
        "username": "Limbo_22",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/d9b06d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-11T22:10:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi,</p><p>I was wondering if it's common amongst the players to read the flavor text outloud when you're playing. When it come to it, Sentinels is basically heavily-based on maths and I think it lights up the game a little when you read the flavor text. I think it reinforce the feeling of actually being the character and it always provides some funny moments.&nbsp;<br><br>When I play with my group of friends, we always read the flavor text outloud and it's fun to see how everyone thinks Legacy should talk or Tempest.</p><p>Currently, were even recording ourselves doing the flavor text on the cards so that when this card enters plays we can, for example, run the audio of Legacy saying: «For liberty...for freedom...for justice...for AMERICA». I usually play with the same groupe of 5 people and we developped some affinities with certain heroes. For example, I'm known to be the voice of Legacy and Omnitron-X, while my friend always read for Tempest.&nbsp;</p><p>If we're not the only one to do it, I was wondering if some of you might find interest in recording voices and sharing them inside the community. It would be so much fun to play audio recordings of someone I don't know doing the voice of The Scholar or Unity.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Let me know what you think about it!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:03.586Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
