        "raw": "<p>Hi,</p><p>I was wondering if it&#39;s common amongst the players to read the flavor text outloud when you&#39;re playing. When it come to it, Sentinels is basically heavily-based on maths and I think it lights up the game a little when you read the flavor text. I think it reinforce the feeling of actually being the character and it always provides some funny moments.&nbsp;<br /><br />When I play with my group of friends, we always read the flavor text outloud and it&#39;s fun to see how everyone thinks Legacy should talk or Tempest.</p><p>Currently, were even recording ourselves doing the flavor text on the cards so that when this card enters plays we can, for example, run the audio of Legacy saying: &laquo;For liberty...for freedom...for justice...for AMERICA&raquo;. I usually play with the same groupe of 5 people and we developped some affinities with certain heroes. For example, I&#39;m known to be the voice of Legacy and Omnitron-X, while my friend always read for Tempest.&nbsp;</p><p>If we&#39;re not the only one to do it, I was wondering if some of you might find interest in recording voices and sharing them inside the community. It would be so much fun to play audio recordings of someone I don&#39;t know doing the voice of The Scholar or Unity.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Let me know what you think about it!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
